{% comment %}
  Renders the options for one filter group, supporting BOTH data sources:

  1. A native Search & Discovery filter (metafield / variant option / product
     attribute). Preferred when present - gives real counts.
  2. Otherwise, a comma-separated tag list - a plain product tag toggled in
     the collection URL's own tag path (/collections/<handle>/tag-a+tag-b).

  Every option here is a real link, applied INSTANTLY on click/tap (no
  separate "Apply" step) - native ones use Shopify's own url_to_add/
  url_to_remove directly (which already preserve every other active filter),
  matching how Size already worked; tag and grouped-colour ones are handled
  by the small vamasInstantFilter() JS in vamas-collection.liquid, which
  merges into the current URL the same way.

  So the merchant can set these up either way (or migrate from tags to
  metafields later) without any theme change.

  Params: native_filter, tag_list, current_tags, empty_note
{% endcomment %}
{% if native_filter != blank %}
  {% if group_colors %}
    {%- comment -%}
      The real Color filter lists every exact variant shade (BOTTLE-GREEN,
      OLIVE-GREEN, DARK-GOLD, COBALT-BLUE...) - 20+ raw options. Grouping them
      under simple families (Green, Blue...) via substring match on the label
      gives a shopper 8-ish broad choices instead. One family link carries
      ALL its real shade values (data-color-values) so clicking it adds/
      removes every one of them at once. Anything that doesn't match a known
      family name still gets its own plain link below, so no colour is ever
      unselectable.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign color_families = 'Black,Maroon,Gold,Green,Navy,Blue,Red,Pink,White,Grey,Purple,Yellow,Orange,Brown,Cream,Beige' | split: ',' -%}
    {%- assign param_name = native_filter.values.first.param_name -%}
    {%- assign assigned_values = '' -%}
    {% for family in color_families %}
      {%- assign family_down = family | downcase -%}
      {%- assign group_values = '' -%}
      {%- assign group_active = false -%}
      {% for value in native_filter.values %}
        {%- assign value_down = value.label | downcase -%}
        {%- if value_down contains family_down -%}
          {%- assign group_values = group_values | append: value.value | append: '||' -%}
          {%- assign assigned_values = assigned_values | append: value.value | append: '||' -%}
          {%- if value.active -%}{%- assign group_active = true -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {% endfor %}
      {% if group_values != '' %}
        <a href="#" class="filter-check-row vcolor-instant{% if group_active %} is-active{% endif %}" data-color-param="{{ param_name }}" data-color-values="{{ group_values }}">
          {{ family }}
        </a>
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% for value in native_filter.values %}
      {%- assign probe = value.value | append: '||' -%}
      {% unless assigned_values contains probe %}
        <a href="{% if value.active %}{{ value.url_to_remove }}{% else %}{{ value.url_to_add }}{% endif %}" class="filter-check-row{% if value.active %} is-active{% endif %}">
          {{ value.label }} ({{ value.count }})
        </a>
      {% endunless %}
    {% endfor %}
  {% else %}
    {% for value in native_filter.values %}
      <a href="{% if value.active %}{{ value.url_to_remove }}{% else %}{{ value.url_to_add }}{% endif %}" class="filter-check-row{% if value.active %} is-active{% endif %}">
        {{ value.label }} ({{ value.count }})
      </a>
    {% endfor %}
  {% endif %}
{% elsif tag_list != blank %}
  {%- comment -%}
    By merchant decision, every value here is independently selectable
    (multi-select OR within this group, e.g. Sleeveless + Full Sleeves both
    at once) rather than the earlier "pick one, replaces the other" pattern.
    This ONLY works via Shopify's filter.p.tag QUERY PARAM (repeated values
    OR together - confirmed live), not the /handle/tag-a+tag-b PATH route
    (which is always AND, impossible for two values of one attribute).
    Trade-off accepted: filter.p.tag has no concept of "this tag belongs to
    Sleeve vs Neckline" - it's one flat bucket, so every group using this
    branch (Sleeve, Neckline, Fabric, Occasion) shares the SAME OR pool.
    Confirmed live: this correctly ANDs with PATH-based tags (Occasion) and
    with native filters (Color/Availability/Price), just not with each
    OTHER - i.e. Sleeveless+V-Neck now means "either", not "both".

    current_tags (path-based) can't see a query-param tag, so is-active
    can't be set here in Liquid - vamasSyncTagActiveState() in vamas-
    collection.liquid reads location.search on load/navigation and adds
    .is-active + rebuilds the removable chips instead.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% assign group_tags = tag_list | split: ',' %}
  {% for t in group_tags %}
    {% assign tag_clean = t | strip %}
    {% if tag_clean != '' %}
      <a href="#" class="filter-check-row vtag-instant" data-tag="{{ tag_clean | escape }}">
        {{ tag_clean }}
      </a>
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
{% else %}
  <p class="filter-empty-note">{{ empty_note | default: 'Not set up yet.' }}</p>
{% endif %}
